  <h2 id="section-6">6. Best Practices for Creating Perfect Round Profile Pictures</h2>
  <p>
    To turn a standard headshot into an engaging, high-impact avatar, follow these professional design and photography principles:
  </p>

  <h3>1. Perfect Eye-Line Alignment and Head Proportions</h3>
  <p>
    Proper composition ensures your face looks balanced within the circle:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>The 60% Rule:</strong> Your head and shoulders should fill roughly 55% to 65% of the total vertical height of the circular canvas.</li>
    <li><strong>Eye Placement:</strong> Position your eyes roughly one-third down from the top edge of the circle. This creates natural, balanced framing.</li>
    <li><strong>Headroom Safety:</strong> Leave a subtle 10% gap above your hair so the top arc of the circle does not shave off your hairstyle.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>2. Select Clean, High-Contrast Backgrounds</h3>
  <p>
    A busy background dilutes focus from your face in compact 40-pixel mobile badges.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Use solid studio backdrops, softly blurred outdoor scenery (bokeh), or architectural textures.</li>
    <li>Ensure sharp contrast between your hair/clothing and the background color.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>3. Prioritize Soft, Front-Facing Lighting</h3>
  <p>
    Even illumination brings out warmth and clarity in the eyes:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Position yourself facing a large window or soft ring light to eliminate harsh under-eye shadows.</li>
    <li>Avoid direct overhead fluorescent lighting or strong backlighting that turns your face into a dark silhouette.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>4. Maintain Direct Eye Contact and Warm Expressions</h3>
  <p>
    Looking directly into the camera lens with an authentic smile or confident expression establishes instant rapport across personal chats and professional networking messages.
  </p>

